### 2. DWDM Interface Parameter YANG
* **Presenter**: Roberto Manzotti
* **Slides**: [01 - A YANG data model to manage configurable DWDM optical interfaces](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/126/materials/slides-126-ccamp-01-a-yang-data-model-to-manage-configurable-dwdm-optical-interfaces-00)
* **Draft**: `draft-ietf-ccamp-dwdm-if-param-yang`
* **Discussion**:
  * Roberto Manzotti presented updates, highlighting alignment with the pluggables gap analysis to add operational parameters, and realigning the model with the Network Management Datastore Architecture (NMDA). A complete JSON example was added to the appendix.
  * Oscar Gonzalez de Dios asked whether there is a relationship with the Inventory (IV) topology work. Roberto Manzotti replied that this is primarily a controller-to-device model, and topology-level mapping should inherit the interface connection. Ramon Casellas agreed.
  * Next steps include addressing a final minor comment regarding default values for read-only data, updating references to RFCs, and proceeding to Working Group Last Call (WGLC).

