### 6. CMIS Access and Control
* **Presenter**: A representative from NTT
* **Slides**: [04-A YANG Data Model for CMIS Access and Control](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/126/materials/slides-126-ccamp-04-a-yang-data-model-for-cmis-access-and-control-00)
* **Discussion**:
  * The presenter introduced a model mirroring the CMIS memory map to handle custom, vendor-specific pages and features not yet natively supported by a network operating system (NOS).
  * Page-level access governance and read-only default policies were added to address security concerns.
  * **Feedback**:
    * Roberto Manzotti questioned whether operators would deploy such low-level register tweaks directly in production networks versus lab environments.
    * Dieter Beller suggested incorporating these requirements into the pluggables drafts rather than maintaining a separate CMIS access draft.
    * Daniele Ceccarelli queried standardizing vendor-specific parameters and suggested the draft might be more suited for the Experimental track.

