### 7. Performance Monitoring Streaming
* **Presenter**: Bin Ye
* **Slides**: [05 - A YANG Data Model for Performance Monitoring Streaming](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/126/materials/slides-126-ccamp-05-a-yang-data-model-for-performance-monitoring-streaming-00)
* **Discussion**:
  * Following coordination with IPPM, the original single draft has been split into three: two generic drafts to be adopted in IPPM and one transport-specific draft in CCAMP.
  * The CCAMP draft defines three groups of PM parameters based on ITU-T G.7710.
  * Daniele Ceccarelli noted that CCAMP must wait for IPPM to adopt the generic foundation drafts before formally adopting the CCAMP extension. Bin Ye agreed to update the draft from Informational to Standards Track. Dieter Beller asked for clarification on the split, which Daniele Ceccarelli explained was necessary to ensure the foundational pieces are generic enough for wider IETF use.

