### 8. Integration of Network Management Agent (NMA) into ACTN
* **Presenter**: Xin Li
* **Slides**: [06-Integration of Network Management Agent (NMA) into ACTN-Based Optical Network](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/126/materials/slides-126-ccamp-06-integration-of-network-management-agent-nma-into-actn-based-optical-network-00)
* **Discussion**:
  * Xin Li presented updates showing coexistence with existing ACTN functions and detailing three deployment scenarios between the MDSC and PNC.
  * Haomian Zheng supported putting the work in the queue but noted the need to track generic NMA framework progress in the IETF. Daniele Ceccarelli agreed but cautioned that CCAMP cannot formally reference the NMA framework until it becomes an adopted work item.
  * Christian Schmutzer questioned the necessity of introducing new "agent" terminology when standard Netconf/YANG mechanisms already handle these interactions. Henry Yu responded that NMA standardizes how AI agents extend ACTN for service assurance and how those agents are managed. Daniele Ceccarelli suggested moving the architectural scope discussion to the mailing list.

