### 9. SLA Assurance Management in Optical Transport Networks
* **Presenter**: Henry Yu
* **Slides**: [07-A YANG Data Model for Service Level Agreement (SLA) Assurance Management in Optical Transport Networks](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/126/materials/slides-126-ccamp-07-a-yang-data-model-for-service-level-agreement-sla-assurance-management-in-optical-transport-networks-00)
* **Discussion**:
  * Henry Yu presented a new model focused on proactive "issue" detection (both symptomatic and asymptomatic) to prevent SLA violations.
  * Daniel King noted that TEAS has active work on service assurance and ACTN POI applicability, and suggested reviewing how this draft aligns with or references TEAS.
  * Haomian Zheng outlined two options: make the model generic in TEAS or focus strictly on Layer 0/1 SLA assurance within CCAMP.
  * Christian Schmutzer pointed out overlap with other standards, such as Mplify, and urged the authors to avoid duplicating existing specifications. Luis Contreras requested the Mplify reference via the chat.

