### 10. OSPF-TE Extensions for Computing Capability Advertisement
* **Presenter**: Yan Xia
* **Slides**: [08 - OSPF-TE Extensions for Computing Capability Advertisement](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/126/materials/slides-126-ccamp-08-ospf-te-extensions-for-computing-capability-advertisement-01)
* **Discussion**:
  * Yan Xia proposed using OSPF-TE to advertise selected AI Data Center (AIDC) compute resources (GPU types, memory, utilization) alongside optical metrics.
  * Daniele Ceccarelli and Adrian Farrel noted that while the application targets optical networks, compute metrics fall under the CATS working group, and routing protocol extensions fall under TEAS/LSR. Adrian Farrel advised the authors to review and align with CATS metric definitions first.
  * Donald Fedyk suggested evaluating the update frequency and distribution of these parameters, as some highly dynamic metrics may not be suitable for OSPF-TE.

