### 11. Optical Networks and AI Computing Orchestration (ONCO)
* **Presenter**: Jun
* **Slides**: [09 - Optical Networks and AI Computing Orchestration (ONCO)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/126/materials/slides-126-ccamp-09-optical-networks-and-ai-computing-orchestration-onco-01)
* **Discussion**:
  * Jun presented architectural updates on coordinating computing schedulers and optical controllers for AI workloads.
  * The presentation mapped ONCO capabilities directly to ACTN architectural components (CNC, MDSC, PNC, CMI, MPI).
  * Daniele Ceccarelli welcomed the clear mapping to ACTN and agreed this approach fits better within CCAMP compared to pure protocol extensions. Haomian Zheng agreed it is a solid starting point for evaluating computational-aware transport.

